From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] qdma: keep the active IRQ mask cached

When NAPI temporarily disables a completion cause, update the cached mask as
well as the hardware register.  Otherwise a later mask update can accidentally
re-enable a cause whose NAPI poll is still active.  This carries the fix from
econet_eth commit 86b755c7a895.

Signed-off-by: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
---
 econet_qdma.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/econet_qdma.c
+++ b/econet_qdma.c
@@ -409,7 +409,8 @@ static irqreturn_t en75_irq_handler(int
					    p.chain);
		}
 
-		en75_wreg(~disable_int, irq->mask_reg[i]);
+		irq->irqmask[i] &= ~disable_int;
+		en75_wreg(irq->irqmask[i], irq->mask_reg[i]);
 	}
 
 	return IRQ_HANDLED;
